name xpunctuate
category Package
revision 67918
shortdesc Process trailing punctuation which may be redundant
relocated 1
longdesc The package provides commands enabling the user (or package
longdesc writer) to insert punctuation after a macro. The method is
longdesc similar to that of xspace, but goes further. The package
longdesc provides the commands \xperiod, \xcomma and \xperiodcomma,
longdesc which follow a similar procedure to that of \xspace, and insert
longdesc punctuation if and only if it is necessary. It also provides
longdesc \xperiodafter, \xcommaafter, \xperiodcommaafter and
longdesc \xspaceafter, which all take one argument, the word or phrase
longdesc to be punctuated. These then avoid problems with the spacing of
longdesc periods and commas after emphasised words.
runfiles size=1
 RELOC/tex/latex/xpunctuate/xpunctuate.sty
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/xpunctuate
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics macro-supp
catalogue-version 2.0
